<title>UK: British Steel up, talk of German steel bid.</title>
<headline>British Steel up, talk of German steel bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Steel Plc rose in pre-market trading on Tuesday, boosted by talk of a takeover in the German steel industry, dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 3p at 157 by 0815 GMT in volume of 108,780 shares.</p>
<p>Thyssen AG said in a statement late on Monday that rival Krupp planned a hostile takeover and that it would use &quot;all approproate measures&quot; to ward off any bid.</p>
<p>Dealers said news of the takeover had a generally positive affect on sentiment in the sector as well as possibly leading to cuts in steel capacity across Europe.</p>
<p>&quot;People are just looking at that bid and the fact that it could mean capacity is taken out,&quot; said one market-maker.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
